 "what_changed": [
  "Texas: two new polls keep Talarico ahead of Paxton (Marist 47–45, UT 50–47); the RCP average is +2.6. Still the hardest of the Democrats' pickups, but it has not slipped.",
  "Maine: Suffolk (Oct 8–11) has Jackson 49–47 over Collins, the third straight poll with Jackson ahead by 2–4. Maine stays the likeliest flip; Collins beat her 2020 polls by 12, so treat a 2-point lead as even.",
  "Iowa: YouGov (Oct 14) Turek 47–46, after Emerson and CNN had Hinson up 2. A true coin flip, and the plus-four math needs it or Kansas.",
  "Kansas: InsiderAdvantage (Oct 11) Hamilton 48–47 and YouGov (Oct 6) 48–45 both have the Democrat narrowly ahead; NYT/Siena had Marshall by 1. Cook's Oct 6 move to Toss Up stands.",
  "Alaska and Michigan: InsiderAdvantage (Oct 11) has Peltola 50–48 and El-Sayed 48–46. Holds in North Carolina (Cooper +14) and Georgia (Ossoff +8) look safe. If those hold, Democrats need four of Maine, Ohio, Texas, Iowa, Kansas, Alaska."
 ],
